# India pack: a blind test on ASCI decisions the pack had not seen (3 Nov 2026).
# Every line is a claim quoted in ASCI's own monthly press release (source URL on each row) for an
# advertisement whose complaint the CCC upheld as misleading or unsubstantiated. Extraction rule, fixed
# before scoring: every numbered case whose stated ground is 'misleading' or '(inadequately) substantiated',
# the claim(s) quoted before that ground, exact duplicates dropped. Some claims are ASCI's English translations.
# set=dev: Nov 2019 + Feb 2020 releases. Scored first with no change (64/148, 43%), then used to write new
#   claim families (pack 2022.3), now 127/148.
# set=heldout: June 2019 release. Not read until the patterns were frozen; scored once: 35/72 (49%);
#   the previous patterns caught 21/72. Do not tune patterns on this set, or it stops being a blind test.
# A case counts as caught when the pack cites any substantiation clause in 'accept'.
